# Anki Rust Conventions

## Required Rust change (v1)

**Per-topic mastery query** — fast stats for eligibility + dashboard at 50k cards.

Deliverables:
- ≥ 3 Rust unit tests
- ≥ 1 Python integration test calling the Rust API
- Undo still works; no collection corruption
- Document touched upstream files + merge difficulty

## Rejected for v1 (unless explicitly requested)

- Rewriting FSRS scheduling logic
- Points-at-stake queue without mastery query shipped first

## Custom data storage

- Performance questions/attempts live in a **separate sidecar `collection.mcat_perf.db`**, kept out of the synced collection (a stock full sync would silently wipe unknown custom tables); cross-device perf sync is a custom uuid-deduped JSON bundle — see `DECISIONS.md` §22
- Performance attempts: **append-only** (avoid sync merge conflicts)
- Revlog conflicts: union entries and recompute FSRS — document the rule

## Performance targets (report via `make bench`)

- Button ack p95 < 50ms; next card p95 < 100ms
- Dashboard first load p95 < 1s; refresh p95 < 500ms

## Python/UI layer

- Call Rust via existing Anki protobuf/PyO3 patterns — do not duplicate scheduling in Python
- Performance mode UI is separate from review screen

## Licensing

AGPL-3.0-or-later. Preserve Anki copyright notices in modified files.
